Article 47 The State may impose border controls, close ports, and take other emergency measures in accordance with relevant laws and regulations in any of the following circumstances:
(a) a war or armed conflict occurs in the vicinity that may affect the security and stability of the national border defense;
(b) a major event occurs that seriously threatens national security or the safety of persons and property of border residents;
(c) the border is seriously threatened by natural disasters, accident disasters, public health incidents, or nuclear, biological, and chemical contamination;
(d) other circumstances that seriously affect the security and stability of the land border and the border area.
The measures specified in the preceding paragraph shall be organized and implemented by the relevant departments of the State Council, relevant military organs, and local people's governments in accordance with relevant laws and regulations.
